  "goodToKnow": "Die Kanzlei is the office of a lawyer, notary or tax adviser: eine Anwaltskanzlei, eine Steuerkanzlei. Originally, it was a chancery, the office of the Kanzler, which is why the head of the German government is called Bundeskanzler and his or her office das Bundeskanzleramt. Mind the stress: kants-LAI, on the final syllable."
